From a037b7ada63fc4f6819a23c4a1454f0a161b161e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 23:04:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06937/11362] [outer-loop] fix E3AgentPolicy.next_move crash on
 a degenerate/empty frame

Found while running exp5587 (a longer/broader HUD-mask cascade check than
any prior E3AgentPolicy test had exercised, budget=400 vs exp5585's 150).
next_move's transition-collection block called
to_logical(grid_of(latest), self.cell) UNGUARDED, while the boundary-events
block a few lines below already wraps its own to_logical call in
try/except Exception: pass for exactly this reason. A degenerate/empty
frame (grid_of(latest) returning shape (0,) -- the same failure class
diagnosed earlier this session in the g50t apply_g50t_label incident, a
post-terminal empty-frame sentinel) made `h, w = grid.shape` raise
ValueError, killing the entire game's remaining action budget with an
unhandled exception on the LIVE SCORED path. This crashed 2 of exp5587's 6
roster games within the first ~400 actions -- not a rare edge case at
realistic budgets.

Fix mirrors the existing defensive pattern already used a few lines below
in the same function: wrap the transition-collection block in
try/except Exception: pass, skipping that one transition record rather
than crashing the game.

Added a regression test reproducing the exact failure (a degenerate frame
following a real one) -- confirmed it fails with the pre-fix code (same
ValueError/traceback) and passes with the fix. Verified zero new
regressions: the 53-file arc_competition_agent regression sweep still
produces the same 10 pre-existing failures / now 337 passed (335 + 2 new
tests), matching the established baseline.

